 "answer": "```cpp\nstd::string read_data(int (*read_func)(void*, void*, size_t, size_t), void* buffer, size_t buffer_size, void* arg) {\n    // Initial attempt with fixed-size buffer\n    char* buf = static_cast<char*>(malloc(buffer_size));\n    size_t bytes_read = read_func(buffer, buf, buffer_size, arg);\n    \n    // Check if the buffer was too small\n    if (bytes_read > buffer_size) {\n        // Dynamically allocate a larger buffer based on the required size\n        size_t new_buffer_size = bytes_read;\n        char* new_buf = static_cast<char*>(malloc(new_buffer_size));\n        \n        // Call the function again with the new buffer\n        bytes_read = read_func(buffer, new_buf, new_buffer_size, arg);\n        \n        // Convert to string\n        if (bytes_read > 0) {\n            return std::string(new_buf, bytes_read);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    // Convert to string with the initial buffer\n    if (bytes_read > 0) {\n        return std::string(buf, bytes_read);\n    }\n    \n    // If read failed or buffer was too small, return empty string\n    free(buf);\n    return \"\";\n}\n```",
